      </div>
      <div style="background:#000;padding:2rem;text-align:center;">
        <div style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:200;color:#e00;margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Pro</div>
        <div style="font-size:0.7rem;letter-spacing:0.1em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#FFFFFF;">Fit Models</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What is Fit Engineering Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Service Overview</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">What Fit Engineering Is</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Fit engineering is the technical process of ensuring garments fit correctly across all sizes and body types. It involves creating fit blocks, testing patterns on fit models, making adjustments based on fit evaluation, and establishing grading rules that maintain consistent proportions from size XS to 5XL.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Fit engineering transforms a design sketch into a garment that fits real bodies. Without proper fit engineering, even beautiful designs can fail in the market due to poor fit. Our fit engineers have decades of experience ensuring garments look and feel right on diverse body types.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Fit Blocks Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Brand Fit</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Fit Blocks and Brand-Specific Fit</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      A fit block is a master pattern that establishes your brand's foundational fit for a garment category | like a basic tee block, dress block, or pant block. Brand-specific fit means developing blocks that reflect your brand's aesthetic and target customer.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Once established, fit blocks enable consistent fit across different styles within your collection and ensure your brand has a recognizable fit signature. Customers come to know and trust your brand's fit, which builds loyalty and reduces returns.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Fit Testing Methodology Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Testing Process</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Fit Testing Methodology</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Our fit testing methodology uses professional fit models representing your target customer demographic. We evaluate garments on measurement forms and live models, assessing ease, balance, proportion, and movement.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      We document fit issues with photos and measurements, then create pattern corrections. Multiple fit rounds ensure the final fit meets your standards. Fit testing happens at prototype stage and again at pre-production sample stage to catch any issues before bulk manufacturing.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Resolving Fit Issues Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Problem Solving</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Resolving Fit Issues</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      We diagnose and resolve fit issues including tightness across bust/chest, gaping at armholes or necklines, pulling at shoulders or hips, sleeve length and circumference problems, and waist-to-hip ratio mismatches.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Our fit engineers identify root causes in the pattern and make precise adjustments to correct the issue without affecting other garment areas. Common fit problems have known solutions that we apply systematically, ensuring corrections are accurate and repeatable.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Plus Size Fit Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Specialized Service</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Plus Size Fit Specialization</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      Plus size fit requires specialized pattern work beyond simple grading. We have plus size fit models and develop patterns specifically for larger body types, accounting for different body proportions, weight distribution, and ease requirements.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      Our plus size engineering ensures garments fit comfortably and flatteringly across extended size ranges. Many brands struggle with plus size fit because they grade up from standard sizes without adjusting for different body proportions. We create dedicated plus size patterns that respect larger bodies.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Fit Consistency Section -->
<section style="padding:5rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid #e00;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header" style="margin-bottom:3rem;">
      <span class="section-label">Quality Assurance</span>
      <div class="accent-line"></div>
      <h2 style="font-size:clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.4rem);font-weight:300;color:#fff;margin-bottom:1rem;">Fit Consistency Across Reorders</h2>
    </div>
    
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;">
      We maintain detailed fit records including approved patterns, measurement charts, and fit samples. For reorders, we reference these records and produce a new fit sample to verify consistency before bulk production.
    </p>
    <p style="color:#FFFFFF;max-width:800px;line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95rem;margin-top:1rem;">
      This ensures your garments fit the same across seasons and production batches, protecting your brand's fit reputation. Customers expect consistency from your brand | fit that changes between orders damages trust and increases returns.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

